    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59466" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κουρ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κουρά</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>for cutting the hair</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχαιραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Dio</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			: as Subst., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κουρικός</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίφρος</span>),
				ὁ, <i>barber's</i> chair, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				4292
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίφρου τετραπόδου καὶ κουρικοῦ ξυλίνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					646
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοῦρος</span> A) <i>like a
				youth.</i>
			Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollon.
					<u>Lex.</u>
				</span></i>
			s.v.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κουρίξ</span>.</div>
